[{:db/id "q-71213/selection/c30d02d69f383c5c280e49b82dc56b093fd6f5acc052ef9d7d103ef659ee73cd" :answer/id #uuid "11867973-a8e0-5370-9271-65bef0969ffa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}+(y-2)^{2}=4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71213/selection/dffa42bc4e1bc56f5087e5a051b3aeecef26a8960977b0e72bc084120e557ca9" :answer/id #uuid "65472bbf-82dd-511b-bc15-fc74b6108845" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y-2=4{x}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71213/selection/b5398d094f0d6f54a19341be7f60ba015a19751802caacfcfb24dd207ddf5b45" :answer/id #uuid "f86d1dc6-7204-5eb1-971c-ccbacf31d7e1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71213/selection/96bcebc9970c151be02ad556c12ed65683e61de57b2880c8cbee41a0a96681d9" :answer/id #uuid "26d6f0e3-d9bb-5b88-a772-65a698498c30" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y-2)^{2}-{x}^{2}=4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71213/selection/cc922f856430f5801e3310ed134e805621725a7e4141e21001050fc1f06a7dbe" :answer/id #uuid "1487a2b1-2a61-5b99-bef3-7ab05e64a212" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4x=\\pm (y-2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71213/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b1e67d35-43a8-5928-9aba-42ff24fbff92" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-71213/selection/c30d02d69f383c5c280e49b82dc56b093fd6f5acc052ef9d7d103ef659ee73cd" :answer-field/choices ["q-71213/selection/c30d02d69f383c5c280e49b82dc56b093fd6f5acc052ef9d7d103ef659ee73cd" "q-71213/selection/dffa42bc4e1bc56f5087e5a051b3aeecef26a8960977b0e72bc084120e557ca9" "q-71213/selection/b5398d094f0d6f54a19341be7f60ba015a19751802caacfcfb24dd207ddf5b45" "q-71213/selection/96bcebc9970c151be02ad556c12ed65683e61de57b2880c8cbee41a0a96681d9" "q-71213/selection/cc922f856430f5801e3310ed134e805621725a7e4141e21001050fc1f06a7dbe"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-71213" :question/id #uuid "b1b4eae9-3493-5eb9-a468-71e6b1cf752c" :question/math-academy-id "q-71213" :question/problem "Find the equation of the level curve that passes through the point $V(2,2)$ for the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{8y}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the value of the function at $V$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(2,2) & =\\frac{8(2)}{{2}^{2}+{2}^{2}}=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the level curve that passes through $V(2,2)$ is the $2$-level curve.\n\nRecall that the level curves for the function $f(x,y)$ are given by the equation\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=c.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we're interested in $c=2.$ So, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =c \\\\ \\frac{8y}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} & =2 \\\\ 4y & ={x}^{2}+{y}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-4y+4 & =4 \\\\ {x}^{2}+(y-2)^{2} & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the level curve that passes through $V(2,2)$ is the circle ${x}^{2}+(y-2)^{2}=4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-71213/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "62dff73b-1857-5192-ae10-fe22577cbfb4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-71213"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-128451/selection/176b79cf1d9a81062e30b56a626aea30a0e433e1007baca568d87760f9ef87dc" :answer/id #uuid "835ba3e7-7076-51e9-87bd-73720884c35e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=3{y}^{2}+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128451/selection/3e4e088b1fa10e0ae6344fa99df59417e96e46a919875a69017d75e64f4d40b4" :answer/id #uuid "44db6d8c-515a-5b7e-be7c-cd2ca2e5de05" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x={y}^{2}+5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128451/selection/f1bdcd1f28c46ef1d9c63d984723415b96d55f53fdfe10b192bd6fc29387d21d" :answer/id #uuid "33881671-7340-5a7a-8e00-837ddbea6379" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=3-{y}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128451/selection/9df91e844e2999e79c41af5f87deed51cbbc3b8b38090a475ca1c62e32ed689f" :answer/id #uuid "7f212c3c-4d87-534a-8095-1d53900b0730" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x={y}^{2}+2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128451/selection/f946826619a0f58b8bc97813edc154abf2c3a139504baa8112e91ca4f69f6190" :answer/id #uuid "63ec9d42-18c1-5718-9ea8-318b7e2bce4e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=1-2{y}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128451/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b24702e2-af21-5fbf-922e-dc8036e0e787" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-128451/selection/9df91e844e2999e79c41af5f87deed51cbbc3b8b38090a475ca1c62e32ed689f" :answer-field/choices ["q-128451/selection/176b79cf1d9a81062e30b56a626aea30a0e433e1007baca568d87760f9ef87dc" "q-128451/selection/3e4e088b1fa10e0ae6344fa99df59417e96e46a919875a69017d75e64f4d40b4" "q-128451/selection/f1bdcd1f28c46ef1d9c63d984723415b96d55f53fdfe10b192bd6fc29387d21d" "q-128451/selection/9df91e844e2999e79c41af5f87deed51cbbc3b8b38090a475ca1c62e32ed689f" "q-128451/selection/f946826619a0f58b8bc97813edc154abf2c3a139504baa8112e91ca4f69f6190"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-128451" :question/id #uuid "e612596d-991d-5ec0-9e3d-c489ec6c2861" :question/math-academy-id "q-128451" :question/problem "Determine the equation of the level curve that passes through the point $P(2,0)$ for the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{1}{x-{y}^{2}+3}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the value of the function at $P:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(2,0) & =\\frac{1}{2-{0}^{2}+3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2-0+3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the level curve that passes through $P(2,0)$ is the $\\frac{1}{5}$-level curve.\n\nRecall that the level curves for the function $f(x,y)$ are given by the equation\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=c.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we're interested in $c=\\frac{1}{5}.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =c \\\\ \\frac{1}{x-{y}^{2}+3} & =\\frac{1}{5} \\\\ 5 & =x-{y}^{2}+3 \\\\ x & ={y}^{2}+2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the level curve that passes through $P(2,0)$ is the parabola $x={y}^{2}+2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-128451/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "62dff73b-1857-5192-ae10-fe22577cbfb4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-128451"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-71192/selection/e92614ed647679eb0196d9f18af13ad077f8ea8324ef8f2d33d5aee3e1186583" :answer/id #uuid "f3e4ee8f-2bbd-52fd-9141-c4dfea7d6f92" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}=23" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71192/selection/6ee0621a5db241c2d1c6bc76a4da0db6b0af3b3b4c4e2459b665949cd3180103" :answer/id #uuid "88a72a83-c01c-54df-a8ff-45be4a0ce1bf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{20}-{y}^{2}=20" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71192/selection/385b1ad7603cf47ffeed97be198ffaf03024ed9f42ef69ec4279cdb3419083d2" :answer/id #uuid "9862426f-4752-50f0-9372-d6e294ac4bfb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}=23" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71192/selection/d85ed517a9382fec1157f37657ae2803ceaee6c4f62c66ae1c021f636475c083" :answer/id #uuid "d5ed5f9d-944f-5241-b766-df0d4a86180c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}=17" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71192/selection/09561b7dad8b702e677a09603142fe5e67c79eb3607f140405a571a0469c2986" :answer/id #uuid "a35a5989-a9ce-55b7-b2c9-746d33be6943" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{20}+{y}^{2}=20" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71192/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3b782891-ba28-528a-8fe7-3ce0b18e2634" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-71192/selection/d85ed517a9382fec1157f37657ae2803ceaee6c4f62c66ae1c021f636475c083" :answer-field/choices ["q-71192/selection/e92614ed647679eb0196d9f18af13ad077f8ea8324ef8f2d33d5aee3e1186583" "q-71192/selection/6ee0621a5db241c2d1c6bc76a4da0db6b0af3b3b4c4e2459b665949cd3180103" "q-71192/selection/385b1ad7603cf47ffeed97be198ffaf03024ed9f42ef69ec4279cdb3419083d2" "q-71192/selection/d85ed517a9382fec1157f37657ae2803ceaee6c4f62c66ae1c021f636475c083" "q-71192/selection/09561b7dad8b702e677a09603142fe5e67c79eb3607f140405a571a0469c2986"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-71192" :question/id #uuid "a94d100b-6a14-57de-a2fd-4d5f54188c98" :question/math-academy-id "q-71192" :question/problem "Find the equation of the level curve that passes through the point $R(3,2)$ for the function $f(x,y)=20-{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the value of the function at $R$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(3,2) & =20-(3)^{2}-2(2)^{2}=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the level curve that passes through $R(3,2)$ is the $3$-level curve.\n\nRecall that the level curves for the function $f(x,y)$ are given by the equation\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=c.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we're interested in $c=3.$ So, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =c \\\\ 20-{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2} & =3 \\\\ {x}^{2}+2{y}^{2} & =17\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the level curve that passes through $R(3,2)$ is the ellipse ${x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}=17.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-71192/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "62dff73b-1857-5192-ae10-fe22577cbfb4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-71192"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-128447/selection/f7729a84b57ba7dcc71127e7ae01453471dd30e4d18e34e798e450f6edaf268e" :answer/id #uuid "a08d6121-a6a1-5e79-ad99-0c8be10fefa5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=2x+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128447/selection/7cdd51955c22b0409896370980a73c8e7f80a78c2673ef1cc2fca938140e8484" :answer/id #uuid "7c060524-8b4c-5f9a-9f2a-04b15c1b7957" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{2}{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128447/selection/f2828f07b83d9a718355f6f154ad27c8f354f4ed674a9ad6fa4431e4c5f838fd" :answer/id #uuid "c07fd626-b5a6-5653-93ad-0822aa402e0c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=x-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128447/selection/06b67cec821aef84e1abc2f7564b06b27d01f1bdd56e1d32712e6ca4a24caef1" :answer/id #uuid "f405929c-6fdb-5231-85fd-d6213baca970" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{x}-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128447/selection/7b9e317a00531c8b82176a43ca6e1e5b6705faa291e73c4b3114aa602ce6947c" :answer/id #uuid "4c4ef1bd-a644-58af-989d-5fdafe5dd3ba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128447/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2a12d53b-9d82-5a92-9335-3e2199cf3707" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-128447/selection/7b9e317a00531c8b82176a43ca6e1e5b6705faa291e73c4b3114aa602ce6947c" :answer-field/choices ["q-128447/selection/f7729a84b57ba7dcc71127e7ae01453471dd30e4d18e34e798e450f6edaf268e" "q-128447/selection/7cdd51955c22b0409896370980a73c8e7f80a78c2673ef1cc2fca938140e8484" "q-128447/selection/f2828f07b83d9a718355f6f154ad27c8f354f4ed674a9ad6fa4431e4c5f838fd" "q-128447/selection/06b67cec821aef84e1abc2f7564b06b27d01f1bdd56e1d32712e6ca4a24caef1" "q-128447/selection/7b9e317a00531c8b82176a43ca6e1e5b6705faa291e73c4b3114aa602ce6947c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-128447" :question/id #uuid "e0e4e5e1-7e08-5442-8bc9-e119961a69a9" :question/math-academy-id "q-128447" :question/problem "Determine the equation of the level curve that passes through the point $P(1,1)$ for the function $f(x,y)=xy-2.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the value of the function at $P:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1,1) & =1(1)-2 \\\\  & =1-2 \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the level curve that passes through $P(1,1)$ is the $-1$-level curve.\n\nRecall that the level curves for the function $f(x,y)$ are given by the equation\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=c.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we're interested in $c=-1.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =c \\\\ xy-2 & =-1 \\\\ xy & =1 \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the level curve that passes through $P(1,1)$ is the hyperbola $y=\\frac{1}{x}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-128447/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "62dff73b-1857-5192-ae10-fe22577cbfb4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-128447"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-36825/selection/3d8684381dc7922ab28ed6544175c8b545ab884ba580a50ecda227d4fff58ec9" :answer/id #uuid "2644416a-2708-5a03-930c-66a23991e6a4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y-1={x}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36825/selection/a5529cdf1409f3cfdeac6d771d2c5d6d3b919af3bdbb977a5e6fa8b49ecd4864" :answer/id #uuid "0eba554c-49d3-502f-8487-efcda0fdf618" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36825/selection/8d98bd6fff070238c71c1beabcd264d1ec97fb434cc445f0f2f42ca504cfeeb8" :answer/id #uuid "17b82f06-5c30-5722-9ec9-52062d470c19" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\pm (y-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36825/selection/f49f7e0a37d20b088381cf57a5d8c8bf76e016503a90ee1a7e088c962f548e33" :answer/id #uuid "bce5cec0-bae9-584d-b30e-58a502515f54" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}+(y-1)^{2}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36825/selection/61844f547ab64b3295c7c8b489f81330f00e486b638f3197acf18be0e981f601" :answer/id #uuid "52df9c01-7d93-5dc5-b6f3-e1973808d10e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y-1)^{2}-{x}^{2}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36825/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0a5648bc-2d5d-50b2-bc64-b499dee8031b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-36825/selection/f49f7e0a37d20b088381cf57a5d8c8bf76e016503a90ee1a7e088c962f548e33" :answer-field/choices ["q-36825/selection/3d8684381dc7922ab28ed6544175c8b545ab884ba580a50ecda227d4fff58ec9" "q-36825/selection/a5529cdf1409f3cfdeac6d771d2c5d6d3b919af3bdbb977a5e6fa8b49ecd4864" "q-36825/selection/8d98bd6fff070238c71c1beabcd264d1ec97fb434cc445f0f2f42ca504cfeeb8" "q-36825/selection/f49f7e0a37d20b088381cf57a5d8c8bf76e016503a90ee1a7e088c962f548e33" "q-36825/selection/61844f547ab64b3295c7c8b489f81330f00e486b638f3197acf18be0e981f601"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-36825" :question/id #uuid "88de5b2b-c4a7-5648-97ab-7bd71becc10f" :question/math-academy-id "q-36825" :question/problem "Find the equation of the level curve that passes through the point $Q(1,1)$ for the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{2y}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the value of the function at $Q$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1,1) & =\\frac{2(1)}{{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the level curve that passes through $Q(1,1)$ is the $1$-level curve.\n\nRecall that the level curves for the function $f(x,y)$ are given by the equation\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=c.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we're interested in $c=1.$ So, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =c \\\\ \\frac{2y}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ 2y & ={x}^{2}+{y}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-2y+1 & =1 \\\\ {x}^{2}+(y-1)^{2} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the level curve that passes through $Q(1,1)$ is the circle ${x}^{2}+(y-1)^{2}=1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-36825/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "62dff73b-1857-5192-ae10-fe22577cbfb4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-36825"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-129062/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "9c00354d-245a-5500-9423-d49cb99f10d3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129062/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "3df6577a-8047-5c16-958a-4a2cafe10ec4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129062/selection/421ba3cf61c86c7d854403490925f53920cd3c015c12342698571d9a74aca2fd" :answer/id #uuid "1e39ed4f-ad18-5a27-8215-107e917124e3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None of the listed" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129062/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "092cadd6-76ef-5345-9ca0-e2da46eb4c50" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129062/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "bcd8cf37-4ab0-583e-ba73-68c28c57b9f6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129062/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f4113bd0-7917-577e-a892-f8a0b96d6965" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-129062/selection/421ba3cf61c86c7d854403490925f53920cd3c015c12342698571d9a74aca2fd" :answer-field/choices ["q-129062/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-129062/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-129062/selection/421ba3cf61c86c7d854403490925f53920cd3c015c12342698571d9a74aca2fd" "q-129062/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-129062/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-129062" :question/id #uuid "0b2cfdd5-7257-5027-8ef3-4d8828269d78" :question/math-academy-id "q-129062" :question/problem "The level curves of the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}$ are given by $f(x,y)=c.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $c=0$ gives a parabola\n- $c=1$ gives an ellipse\n- $c=2$ gives a hyperbola" :question/worked-solution "Setting $f(x,y)=c$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} & =c \\\\ {y}^{2} & =c({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}) \\\\ c{x}^{2}+(c-1){y}^{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n- If $c=0,$ the level curve is the line $y=0,$ which is the $x$-axis. So, I is false.\n\n- If $c=1,$ the level curve is the line $x=0,$ which is the $y$-axis. So, II is false.\n\n- If $c=2,$  then we obtain \n\n$$\n\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}=2\\,⟹\\,2{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=0.\n$$\n\nHowever, the only real solution to this equation is  $(x,y)=(0,0),$ which is not in the domain of $f(x,y)$ because it would result in division by zero. Thus, III is false.\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"None of the listed\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-129062/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74f126da-5f3b-5af8-9aee-d6f0a4c61c49"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-129062"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-71391/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "eee63a1d-98d4-5e84-ab26-ff7cd9428d66" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71391/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "a750f04d-4cf1-50ef-90c2-95f6c8366994" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71391/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "acd04519-a14e-5a48-aa69-c4da3afa7257" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71391/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "76214168-f2f5-511f-95d8-2b38da4025ea" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71391/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "aac0359d-5ee4-5610-b651-6924e0ef731f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71391/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ea178ba4-3b2d-56d1-a758-c52013fee9fa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-71391/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer-field/choices ["q-71391/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-71391/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-71391/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-71391/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-71391/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-71391" :question/id #uuid "f59b0ead-9e6c-5643-b77d-cab71602ea67" :question/math-academy-id "q-71391" :question/problem "The level curves of the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{2{x}^{2}+3{y}^{2}-4}{{y}^{2}}$ are given by $f(x,y)=c.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $c=3$ gives a hyperbola\n- $c=0$ gives an ellipse\n- $c=1$ gives a circle" :question/worked-solution "Setting $f(x,y)=c$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2{x}^{2}+3{y}^{2}-4}{{y}^{2}} & =c \\\\ 2{x}^{2}+3{y}^{2}-4 & =c{y}^{2} \\\\ 2{x}^{2}+(3-c){y}^{2} & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n- If $c=3$ then the level curves are $x=\\pm \\sqrt{2},$ which consists of two vertical lines.\n\n- If $c=0$ then the level curve is $2{x}^{2}+3{y}^{2}=4,$ which is an ellipse.\n\n- If $c=1$ then the level curve is ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=2,$ which is a circle.\n\nSo, only statements II and III are true." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-71391/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74f126da-5f3b-5af8-9aee-d6f0a4c61c49"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-71391"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-71401/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "6af2192e-586c-58b7-b496-2ab6ceb51e59" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71401/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "60be151f-5f4f-55ed-b86a-55fabdbd0c4d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71401/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "918433c3-8692-5f7b-a566-0915929ea1e3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71401/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "e1b6b5cc-162b-5edd-bb4f-59471b51d7c2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71401/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "aeb3ebb9-9f1c-55c8-b68d-0de69cca94a4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71401/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "bd203f7d-7b45-5f00-9764-ace8d438c59c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-71401/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer-field/choices ["q-71401/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-71401/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-71401/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-71401/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-71401/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-71401" :question/id #uuid "89b4a109-08c5-568a-830b-41c72ba008a5" :question/math-academy-id "q-71401" :question/problem "The level curves of the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{2{y}^{2}+1}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}$ are given by $f(x,y)=c.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $c=1$ gives an ellipse\n- $c=2$ gives two lines\n- $c=3$ gives a hyperbola" :question/worked-solution "Setting $f(x,y)=c$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2{y}^{2}+1}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} & =c \\\\ 2{y}^{2}+1 & =c({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}) \\\\ c{x}^{2}+(c-2){y}^{2} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n- If $c=1$ then the level curve is ${x}^{2}-{y}^{2}=1,$ which is a hyperbola.\n\n- If $c=2$ then the level curves are $x=\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},$ which consists of two vertical lines.\n\n- If $c=3$ then the level curve is $3{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1,$ which is an ellipse.\n\nSo, only statement II is true." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-71401/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74f126da-5f3b-5af8-9aee-d6f0a4c61c49"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-71401"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-129063/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "edee10e6-dadf-5e6c-835d-6d1b8b4a6b94" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129063/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "4f1e7267-29ec-5502-90c3-2199591c3532" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129063/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "ecd26afd-4e19-5316-b8b9-244d9ce7bada" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129063/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "2856fae1-b7d3-541a-8de1-d1a46c0b3f71" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129063/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "488f8b49-e1a6-5201-ab51-c167e92e4b52" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129063/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "34084d4a-95f3-5afc-992f-eb0618f1942d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-129063/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer-field/choices ["q-129063/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-129063/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-129063/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-129063/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-129063/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-129063" :question/id #uuid "c65929ca-a9b2-5ccd-885b-e20eab37e456" :question/math-academy-id "q-129063" :question/problem "The level curves of the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{y}{x}$ are given by $f(x,y)=c.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $c=-1$ gives a hyperbola\n- $c=0$ gives the $y$-axis, excluding the origin\n- $c=1$ gives the line $y=x,$ excluding the origin" :question/worked-solution "Setting $f(x,y)=c$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y}{x} & =c \\\\ y & =cx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n- If $c=-1,$ the level curve is the line $y=-x,$ excluding the origin. So, I is false.\n\n- If $c=0,$ the level curve is the line $y=0,$ which is the $x$-axis (excluding the origin). So, II is false.\n\n- If $c=1,$ the level curve is the line $y=x,$ excluding the origin. So, III is true.\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"III only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-129063/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74f126da-5f3b-5af8-9aee-d6f0a4c61c49"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-129063"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-129058/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "841e4a70-803f-5f58-b9a3-667f0ffdffc8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129058/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "8e97890f-697a-510b-99ac-d22dc40f883b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129058/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "e4e4d524-165c-5206-b7e8-72fead25c64b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129058/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "aad28799-dcb3-53ea-9f39-f2520336bd8f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129058/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "ba8018a8-f1f3-511e-b66a-29289a09a885" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129058/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8088bee8-b3a8-5533-b92d-aa613e6a4a89" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-129058/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer-field/choices ["q-129058/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-129058/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-129058/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-129058/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-129058/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-129058" :question/id #uuid "56b2dc5a-8a55-52b8-86dd-0056a08fe2fa" :question/math-academy-id "q-129058" :question/problem "The level curves of the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{x+{y}^{2}}{x}$ are given by $f(x,y)=c.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $c=-1$ gives a line\n- $c=0$ gives a parabola, excluding the origin\n- $c=1$ gives the $x$-axis, excluding the origin" :question/worked-solution "Setting $f(x,y)=c$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x+{y}^{2}}{x} & =c \\\\ x+{y}^{2} & =cx \\\\ x(1-c)+{y}^{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n- If $c=-1,$ the level curve is $x=-\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2},$ which is a parabola that opens to the left (excluding the origin). So, I is false.\n\n- If $c=0,$ the level curves is $x=-{y}^{2},$ which is a parabola that opens to the left (excluding the origin). So, II is true.\n\n- If $c=1,$ the level curve is $y=0,$ which is the $x$-axis (excluding the origin). So, III is true.\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II and III only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-129058/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74f126da-5f3b-5af8-9aee-d6f0a4c61c49"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-129058"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-64909/selection/289a5f11184caa888752d52e596cfff47001c7a64ca206f3cfb50e6575451218" :answer/id #uuid "5e55dc49-24f9-5af9-97cd-895a5ccc1ed3" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042279/assets/57f87a716b14698d0087bc65e9abdc04776bd4b7addaaf172a4e5f0a5f38ea6a.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64909/selection/6a76e88f12ff12589b95c833d74615d6b7c40fe21f68fa8e714a6434c2bae1f8" :answer/id #uuid "2735966f-9783-5290-9cf9-d4434b337ca1" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042279/assets/d330ddb12d1df9d31af3d082b04271d02df381739064a6fe2203dabce358a09f.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64909/selection/e04d09762fed65080d3c93c4fdb50f6fc9744b119bd79bb6921e4e8e9e56edfa" :answer/id #uuid "5220b7e6-a9f1-5521-94d6-7b605f285077" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042279/assets/836e10a411261b1ef2cb8146aed75c40326f278487e5843c57f10f65b9cc3f05.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64909/selection/9625c84ed881d9baf886122edf48b4f2c0b5f434df9146473a419cadb6c91b37" :answer/id #uuid "40b3212b-c714-502c-a01d-763a17dceaaa" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042279/assets/24b6123a1f641df32cdc19ec77d999dac5584b9693ae92ce9c1e618f67487473.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64909/selection/f004a2fe3414ba7f0eff1e2a25fc4b7cc1d0f24a930dd5975b0b3d69f454a14d" :answer/id #uuid "ee81be0a-29bf-502b-a54a-142313c32252" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042279/assets/ef3171d89bff6a2a6ef105f81a9fe60959f2d760634039cd8fb0f70cf8c2cc9e.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64909/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ff473d8e-0f42-5030-81e1-4037a4f4b557" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-64909/selection/6a76e88f12ff12589b95c833d74615d6b7c40fe21f68fa8e714a6434c2bae1f8" :answer-field/choices ["q-64909/selection/289a5f11184caa888752d52e596cfff47001c7a64ca206f3cfb50e6575451218" "q-64909/selection/6a76e88f12ff12589b95c833d74615d6b7c40fe21f68fa8e714a6434c2bae1f8" "q-64909/selection/e04d09762fed65080d3c93c4fdb50f6fc9744b119bd79bb6921e4e8e9e56edfa" "q-64909/selection/9625c84ed881d9baf886122edf48b4f2c0b5f434df9146473a419cadb6c91b37" "q-64909/selection/f004a2fe3414ba7f0eff1e2a25fc4b7cc1d0f24a930dd5975b0b3d69f454a14d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-64909" :question/id #uuid "2e086daf-480c-5185-b9b5-74c8b16950ea" :question/math-academy-id "q-64909" :question/problem "Which of the following represents the level curves of $f(x,y)={e}^{xy}?$" :question/worked-solution "The level curves for the function $f(x,y)$ are given by the equations \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=c.\n$$\n\nNotice that the range of $f(x,y)$ is $(0,\\infty ).$ So, we will consider only level curves for $c>0.$\n\nTherefore, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =c \\\\ {e}^{xy} & =c \\\\ xy & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡c \\\\ y & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡c}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can split this into three cases, depending on the sign of $\\operatorname{ln}⁡c.$\n\n- Case 1: $\\operatorname{ln}⁡c>0.$ In this case, we have the family of hyperbolas $y=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡c}{x}.$\n\n- Case 2: $\\operatorname{ln}⁡c=0.$ In this case, we have the lines $x=0$ and $y=0.$\n\n- Case 3: $\\operatorname{ln}⁡c<0.$ In this case, we have the family of hyperbolas $y=-\\frac{|\\operatorname{ln}⁡c|}{x}.$\n\nThe equation above gives us a family of hyperbolas centered at the origin. Therefore, the correct graph is as follows:\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042279/assets/d330ddb12d1df9d31af3d082b04271d02df381739064a6fe2203dabce358a09f.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-64909/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dfd8982d-d859-5eb2-9f35-69af39c04822"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-64909"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-71409/selection/60671dcfcefd9003106569646ad991ff98d1e676d0972451484b8b66f9f00985" :answer/id #uuid "0ca4c656-4024-5fa8-9886-72d9d2e141f0" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042279/assets/6521da99a82e38a68a5aa87a0c7c88eacf4ed7b78351af594ec309fa2cb7f57b.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71409/selection/d883588444e419b2df90ca89b727ed3bb1e7f37ce31ae37353771bd151fee3e5" :answer/id #uuid "a6b6d3da-5157-5610-bb69-8d6381907d98" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042279/assets/cccaa6d7f554076b3a79364e1f2c4c061ae7cd86f7f0064e3861ba3b035b6a3e.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71409/selection/e07178ee31f8134d230229f177b8075044a28a4c6b495cd71543e3997089a72c" :answer/id #uuid "7aa21f66-073d-567d-9f71-2ea69e94848b" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042279/assets/7ab95ed367277627d5baf535db74994d7d02cd41deae939d76ed08e22799ff40.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71409/selection/b9d3c7c19b85a5f9ce54f1199a82ef4af9f6a206d0092a6dda27389bdd998368" :answer/id #uuid "457284a8-64f6-5680-945b-33a6fc919dfc" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042279/assets/7c4530dc74747fc0bdae0ca4c8608a72dbf03ca413d4479c8a4b9224246ac01f.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71409/selection/a114341db6db92eb8d270ce7d03ee0865fcb51d39bdc8dad7c234c4861d9d8b8" :answer/id #uuid "1b4b7fcb-eef5-5e73-8a41-f4e1f8753371" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042279/assets/1b1cd5983d4a19990cc5e82726bb8cd8101dbab0f2dc7c9934a64c45e6126ee4.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71409/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "723057bd-827e-5d93-838a-760198ad902f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-71409/selection/d883588444e419b2df90ca89b727ed3bb1e7f37ce31ae37353771bd151fee3e5" :answer-field/choices ["q-71409/selection/60671dcfcefd9003106569646ad991ff98d1e676d0972451484b8b66f9f00985" "q-71409/selection/d883588444e419b2df90ca89b727ed3bb1e7f37ce31ae37353771bd151fee3e5" "q-71409/selection/e07178ee31f8134d230229f177b8075044a28a4c6b495cd71543e3997089a72c" "q-71409/selection/b9d3c7c19b85a5f9ce54f1199a82ef4af9f6a206d0092a6dda27389bdd998368" "q-71409/selection/a114341db6db92eb8d270ce7d03ee0865fcb51d39bdc8dad7c234c4861d9d8b8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-71409" :question/id #uuid "94f47fe3-89d1-5943-be21-5cabcd5b8b5e" :question/math-academy-id "q-71409" :question/problem "Which of the following represents the level curves of $f(x,y)=\\sqrt{3{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}}?$" :question/worked-solution "The level curves for the function $f(x,y)$ are given by the equations \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=c.\n$$\n\nNotice that the range of $f(x,y)$ is $[0,\\infty ).$ So, we will consider only level curves for $c\\ge 0.$\n\nTherefore, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =c \\\\ \\sqrt{3{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}} & =c \\\\ 3{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2} & ={c}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation above gives us a family of ellipses centered at the origin. Therefore, the correct graph is as follows:\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042279/assets/cccaa6d7f554076b3a79364e1f2c4c061ae7cd86f7f0064e3861ba3b035b6a3e.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-71409/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dfd8982d-d859-5eb2-9f35-69af39c04822"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-71409"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-64908"] :question/problem "Which of the following represents the level curves of $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(y-2{x}^{2})?$" :question/worked-solution "The level curves for the function $f(x,y)$ are given by the equations \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=c.\n$$\n\nNotice that the range of $f(x,y)$ is $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ So, we will consider level curves for any value of $c.$\n\nTherefore, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =c \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(y-2{x}^{2}) & =c \\\\ y-2{x}^{2} & ={e}^{c} \\\\ y & =2{x}^{2}+{e}^{c}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation above gives us a family of parabolas with the vertex at $(0,{e}^{c}).$ Therefore, the correct graph is as follows:\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042279/assets/6521da99a82e38a68a5aa87a0c7c88eacf4ed7b78351af594ec309fa2cb7f57b.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-129116/selection/d62aedc5a0ba5e21ad2aa6dac67bd6c24d40f0621698b9f4cc6b89ff77babe54" :answer/id #uuid "2d320065-896c-59e5-a66b-0332de590f38" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042279/assets/d5e28121cd5847f3119a9fb33a57dd2d86e2f12bff3061ef64182b12c1ace178.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129116/selection/b3da26bba035bb05dad15d7d9eb7c5c365fb38c4c0615bba277e228442d0ce57" :answer/id #uuid "9a29ba99-6f02-511a-a252-ca34e48a8196" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042279/assets/5155660bc0e9957b1a33cc6fbd933ba10618be07911f9384255bc703f7925ba7.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate