{:db/id "q-129116" :question/id #uuid "384942ae-d22a-5af8-bd31-df40d8002920" :question/math-academy-id "q-129116" :question/problem "Which of the following represents the level curves of $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(y-x)?$" :question/worked-solution "The level curves for the function $f(x,y)$ are given by the equations \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=c.\n$$\n\nNotice that the range of $f(x,y)$ is $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ So, we will consider level curves for any value of $c.$\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =c \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(y-x) & =c \\\\ y-x & ={e}^{c} \\\\ y & =x+{e}^{c}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation above gives us a family of lines with slope of $1.$ Also, note that ${e}^{c}>0$ for all $c.$ Therefore, the correct graph is as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042279/assets/c115999648577bfb60015f0e54dd0c6d6de22076e87026ba94c49e56207144e0.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-129116/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dfd8982d-d859-5eb2-9f35-69af39c04822"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-129116"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-129113/selection/6264c3f42e1122069ba06190c2158abff859dfe6657463270aa3945cbf77214d" :answer/id #uuid "42470d2d-949a-5a29-9611-e905640c69e1" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042279/assets/cdd8cec2d30ff2956d5210a49036c17d99781d0b62c0b0f42f97d0575c4d80f6.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129113/selection/a48c5675d28b49015b42c2ba895754f4b7884f896eb1601ee2a1f30821cde6e0" :answer/id #uuid "fee1319c-849e-538d-ad07-70e5e27fb1a8" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042279/assets/67e9cfee7779fdde389a0804e7f52372ca9434de56b6611d296d4ac9c0759f72.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129113/selection/21eb5cee1307f2b1eed856afd5788b28e9f93fcd59208481caa4da40ab12decb" :answer/id #uuid "fed47638-bb09-57ed-a33f-cd98976291b1" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042279/assets/d774c444ad33c68ec5d507611324030f2005671265ba5f855f322d8db57b69b4.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129113/selection/fd7985808c1608215523785e6a473e05a7fd1f62a0fcc18eaea0d6821d7537e0" :answer/id #uuid "73fb89e3-4034-5594-82dd-72bdb1a64ca4" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042279/assets/2c570cc9958db69a30dc400920b6ff27574e79bd26a53b35e086cb03034c5b6d.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129113/selection/8aea138652387d89e548663985f0c119ed0dfc1f62d50e09e9ee3805f224ed04" :answer/id #uuid "63750657-b5b7-5a30-859d-cff0a5ded1a6" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042279/assets/ef27f12eb1ee6872210bf8cadb6908efd31c1bb54e9e7d34cc3456df2ee03a77.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129113/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6da9e415-1b08-5085-a961-0a9b17583025" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-129113/selection/6264c3f42e1122069ba06190c2158abff859dfe6657463270aa3945cbf77214d" :answer-field/choices ["q-129113/selection/6264c3f42e1122069ba06190c2158abff859dfe6657463270aa3945cbf77214d" "q-129113/selection/a48c5675d28b49015b42c2ba895754f4b7884f896eb1601ee2a1f30821cde6e0" "q-129113/selection/21eb5cee1307f2b1eed856afd5788b28e9f93fcd59208481caa4da40ab12decb" "q-129113/selection/fd7985808c1608215523785e6a473e05a7fd1f62a0fcc18eaea0d6821d7537e0" "q-129113/selection/8aea138652387d89e548663985f0c119ed0dfc1f62d50e09e9ee3805f224ed04"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-129113" :question/id #uuid "2022b58f-f48d-5794-93ee-d709576b1e72" :question/math-academy-id "q-129113" :question/problem "Which of the following represents the level curves of $f(x,y)=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x?$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the range of $f(x,y)$ is $[-3,3].$ So, we will consider only $c$-level curves for $c\\in [-3,3].$\n\nThe level curves for the function $f(x,y)$ are given by the equations \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=c\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =c \\\\ 3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =c \\\\ x & =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡\\frac{c}{3}+2\\pi n,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ can be any integer. \n\nNotice that the equations $x=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡\\frac{c}{3}+2\\pi n$ do not depend on $y.$ So, for a given $c\\in [-3,3]$ and integer $n$, the right-hand side of the equation is constant. As a result, we obtain a family of vertical lines, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042279/assets/cdd8cec2d30ff2956d5210a49036c17d99781d0b62c0b0f42f97d0575c4d80f6.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-129113/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dfd8982d-d859-5eb2-9f35-69af39c04822"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-129113"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-5968"] :question/problem "Find the equation of the level curve that passes through the point $G\\big(\\sqrt{5}, 1\\big)$ for the function $f(x,y) = \\dfrac{12y}{x^2-y^2}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the value of the function at $G$:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n  f\\big(\\sqrt{5}, 1\\big)&= \\dfrac{12(1)}{\\big(\\sqrt{5}\\big)^2 - 1^2} = 3}\n$$\n\nHence, the level curve that passes through $G\\big(\\sqrt{5}, 1\\big)$ is the $3$-level curve.\n\nRecall that the level curves for the function $f(x,y)$ are given by the equation\n\n$$\nf(x,y) = c.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we're interested in $c=3.$ So, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =c \\\\ \\frac{12y}{{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}} & =3 \\\\ 4y & ={x}^{2}-{y}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2}-{y}^{2}-4y-4 & =-4 \\\\ {x}^{2}-({y}^{2}+4y+4) & =-4 \\\\ {x}^{2}-(y+2)^{2} & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the level curve that passes through $G\\big(\\sqrt{5}, 1\\big)$ is the hyperbola $x^2 - (y+2)^2 = -4.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4228"] :question/problem "The level curves of the function $f(x,y) = \\dfrac{x^2+2y^2-2}{x^2}$ are given by $f(x,y) = c.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $c=1$ gives a circle\n\n- $c=0$ gives an ellipse\n\n- $c=2$ gives a hyperbola" :question/worked-solution "Setting $f(x,y) = c$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}-2}{{x}^{2}} & =c \\\\ {x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}-2 & =c{x}^{2} \\\\ (1-c){x}^{2}+2{y}^{2} & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n- If $c = 1,$ then the level curve is $y^2 = 1,$ which consists of two lines.\n\n- If $c = 0,$ then the level curve is $x^2+2y^2=2,$ which is an ellipse.\n\n- If $c = 2,$ then the level curve is $2y^2-x^2=2$ which is a hyperbola.\n\nSo, only statements II and III are true." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4229"] :question/problem "Sketch the level curves of the surface $z=e^{x^2-y^2}.$" :question/worked-solution "The level curves for the function $f(x,y)=e^{x^2-y^2}$ take the form\n\n$$\ne^{x^2-y^2} = c.\n$$\n\nNote that we must have the constraint $c\\gt 0$ since $e^x \\gt 0$ for all $x.$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}=c \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}})=\\operatorname{ln}⁡c \\\\ {x}^{2}-{y}^{2}=\\operatorname{ln}⁡c.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can split this into three cases, depending on the sign of $\\ln c.$\n\n- Case 1: $\\ln c \\gt 0.$ In this case, we have the family of hyperbolas $x^2-y^2 = \\ln c.$\n\n- Case 2: $\\ln c = 0.$ In this case, we have the lines $y=\\pm x.$\n\n- Case 3: $\\ln c < 0.$ In this case, we have the family of hyperbolas $y^2 - x^2 = -\\ln c.$\n\nTherefore, the level curves are as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042279/assets/5f2ec43639cb31e03cc4a00e43969c7f0333c098fc4b366ea1609772faabfda5.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
